{"id":52222,"ord":10,"n_segments":181,"prev":52221,"next":52223,"doc":{"id":"67256","title":"67256_Paul L. Howard oral history interview","collection":"rutgers","inst":"Rutgers — Institute of Jazz Studies","interviewee":"Paul L. Howard","interviewer":"","date":"","year":"","source_url":"https://rucore.libraries.rutgers.edu/rutgers-lib/67256/","url":"https://thisismattmiller.github.io/linked-jazz-2026-transcripts/?t=67256"},"chapter":"Opening, arrival in Los Angeles and the Quality Four","title":"The Black and Tan Orchestra and its members","category":"band_or_employer","summary":"Howard names Harry Sutherland as leader and James Jackson and Papa Mutt Carey among the players; Reb Spikes never played with them.","period":"early 1920s","year_from":1920,"year_to":1923,"words":98,"start":[16,17],"end":[17,16],"url":"https://thisismattmiller.github.io/linked-jazz-2026-transcripts/?t=67256#s52222","tags":{"places":[],"venues":[],"bands":[{"name":"Black and Tan Orchestra","focus":1,"leader":"Harry Sutherland"}]},"people":[{"name":"Mutt Carey","qid":"Q356078","n":7},{"name":"Reb Spikes","qid":"Q7301582","n":3},{"name":"James Jackson","qid":null,"n":1},{"name":"Harry Sutherland","qid":null,"n":1}],"story":{"theme":34,"theme_name":"Who was in the band: naming sidemen and personnel","community":60,"community_name":"Who played in the band: reciting personnel","core":true},"blocks":[{"p":16,"b":17,"s":"MR. COLLETTE","x":"Yeah, that's coming up."},{"p":17,"b":0,"s":"MR. HOWARD","x":"Long time ago. Black and tan."},{"p":17,"b":1,"s":"MR. COLLETTE","x":"Do you remember -- okay."},{"p":17,"b":2,"s":"MS. WILLARD","x":"Who led the Black and Tan? Who was the leader?"},{"p":17,"b":3,"s":"MR. HOWARD","x":"Harry Sutherland."},{"p":17,"b":4,"s":"MS. WILLARD","x":"And you were part of that."},{"p":17,"b":5,"s":"MR. HOWARD","x":"Uh-huh."},{"p":17,"b":6,"s":"MS. WILLARD","x":"Who else was in that orchestra?"},{"p":17,"b":7,"s":"MR. HOWARD","x":"James Jackson, and -- what's -- Papa Mudson?"},{"p":17,"b":8,"s":"MR. COLLETTE","x":"Papa Mutt?"},{"p":17,"b":9,"s":"MR. HOWARD","x":"Papa Mutt."},{"p":17,"b":10,"s":"MR. COLLETTE","x":"Mutt Carey, isn't it?"},{"p":17,"b":11,"s":"MR. HOWARD","x":"Yeah."},{"p":17,"b":12,"s":"MR. COLLETTE","x":"Carey, what's his name? Mutt Carey?"},{"p":17,"b":13,"s":"MR. HOWARD","x":"Yeah, Mutt Carey. And there was somebody else in that band. I can't think of the one."},{"p":17,"b":14,"s":"MS. HOWARD","x":"Reb Spikes."},{"p":17,"b":15,"s":"MR. COLLETTE","x":"Reb Spikes? Was he in there?"},{"p":17,"b":16,"s":"MR. HOWARD","x":"No, uh-huh. Reb never played with us. He got mad."}]}